ase_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:53bdaafd7de38f1996f18eb3414c4c19a392434aa81066ef000e099785f197c9","file":"preprints/Global-classical-solutions-of-the-three-dimensional-relativistic-Vlasov-Maxwell-system-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":42,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"2a7dc57652a5ebaf7480fc94a29de1f29fa2afd1ae391e1c5e6d56c37644bccb","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Global-classical-solutions-of-the-three-dimensional-relativistic-Vlasov-Maxwell-system-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:53bdaafd7de38f1996f18eb3414c4c19a392434aa81066ef000e099785f197c9","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Global-classical-solutions-of-the-three-dimensional-relativistic-Vlasov-Maxwell-system-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L42"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:global}\nEvery smooth admissible datum \\eqref{eq:data} generates a unique global\nclassical solution of \\eqref{eq:rvm}. For every finite $T$, this solution\nsatisfies\n\\[\n f\\in C^\\infty([0,T]\\times\\R^3_x\\times\\R^3_v),\\qquad\n E,B\\in C^\\infty([0,T]\\times\\R^3_x;\\R^3),\n\\]\nand $f$ has compact phase-space support on $[0,T]$.\nThe two divergence constraints hold for all time."}
